  {
    "runtag": "cfda-chiq-llm4cs-splade-rrf",
    "type": "ikat-dialog-v1",
    "topic": "8-1",
    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m actually looking for ways to manage ADHD at work. What are some general strategies?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can ADHD be managed?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Here are some effective strategies to manage ADHD at work:\n\n1. **Organize Your Workspace**: Maintain a clutter-free area with designated spots for supplies to minimize distractions.\n\n2. **Use Headphones**: Block out distracting noises with headphones playing white noise or calming music.\n\n3. **Take Breaks**: Schedule regular breaks to help manage hyperactivity and maintain focus.\n\n4. **Keep Notes**: Use a notepad to jot down important points during meetings and to track tasks, which can help with forgetfulness.\n\n5. **Limit Over-Scheduling**: Avoid taking on too many tasks at once. Break projects into smaller, manageable parts and set realistic deadlines.\n\n6. **Request Accommodations**: If needed, consider asking for a quiet workspace or flexible hours to better suit your needs.\n\n7. **Practice Good Sleep Hygiene**: Ensure you're getting quality sleep, as lack of rest can worsen ADHD symptoms.\n\n8. **Set Up Reminders**: Use electronic reminders for appointments and deadlines to help manage time effectively.\n\nBy implementing these strategies, you can create a more conducive work environment for managing your ADHD symptoms.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0033-18-04361:18": 3.726545572280884,
            "clueweb22-en0019-85-03855:10": 3.692505121231079,
            "clueweb22-en0025-75-16053:1": 3.5554566383361816,
