      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Nice, I see. How do you stay attentive in meetings with ADHD?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to stay attentive in meetings while having ADHD?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Staying attentive in meetings with ADHD can be challenging, but here are some effective strategies to help you focus:\n\n1. **Take Notes**: Jotting down key points can keep your mind engaged and provide a physical outlet for restlessness.\n\n2. **Set Clear Objectives**: Before the meeting, outline what you want to achieve. This gives you a purpose and helps maintain focus.\n\n3. **Use Technology**: Consider using tools like a timer or reminders to keep track of time and stay on task during discussions.\n\n4. **Engage Actively**: Ask questions or contribute to discussions to keep your mind engaged and prevent drifting off.\n\n5. **Limit Distractions**: If possible, choose a seat away from distractions and use noise-cancelling headphones or earplugs to minimize background noise.\n\n6. **Practice Mindfulness**: Techniques such as deep breathing can help ground you and refocus your attention when you feel distracted.\n\n7. **Request Shorter Meetings**: If possible, advocate for brief meetings, as shorter durations can help maintain your concentration.\n\nBy integrating these strategies, you can enhance your ability to stay attentive and participate effectively in meetings.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0019-85-03855:11": 1.2807468175888062,
            "clueweb22-en0008-61-11890:3": 0.0955476388335228
          },
