          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That sounds effective. What if a person with ADHD is in hyperfocus\u2014how can they handle distractions during that intense state?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can a person with ADHD handle distractions while in hyperfocus?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "When someone with ADHD is in a state of hyperfocus, handling distractions can be challenging. Here are some strategies to manage that intense focus effectively:\n\n1. **Set Timers**: Use a timer to create intervals for focused work. This can help signal when it's time to take a break or switch tasks, preventing prolonged hyperfocus.\n\n2. **Physical Breaks**: If you notice distractions creeping in, take a brief walk or do a quick chore in another room. This can help reset your focus.\n\n3. **Visual Reminders**: Place visible cues in your workspace to remind you of other tasks or breaks you need to take. This can help you transition out of hyperfocus when necessary.\n\n4. **Enlist Support**: Ask a colleague or friend to gently remind you to shift your attention if they notice you\u2019re too engrossed in one task. \n\n5. **Scheduled Downtime**: Plan specific times for breaks or check-ins throughout your work session to ensure you\u2019re not losing track of other responsibilities.\n\nBy implementing these strategies, you can better manage your hyperfocus and reduce the likelihood of distractions becoming overwhelming.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0034-01-04061:10": 2.611696243286133,
            "clueweb22-en0019-85-03855:11": 2.537656545639038,
            "clueweb22-en0034-01-04061:15": 2.074429512023926,
