  {
    "runtag": "cfda-chiq-llm4cs-splade-rrf",
    "type": "ikat-fragment-v1",
    "topic": "8-1",
    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Nice, I see. How do you stay attentive in meetings with ADHD?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to stay attentive in meetings while having ADHD?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Staying attentive in meetings with ADHD can be challenging, but here are some effective strategies to help you focus:\n\n1. **Take Notes**: Jotting down key points can keep your mind engaged and provide a physical outlet for restlessness.\n\n2. **Set Clear Objectives**: Before the meeting, outline what you want to achieve. This gives you a purpose and helps maintain focus.\n\n3. **Use Technology**: Consider using tools like a timer or reminders to keep track of time and stay on task during discussions.\n\n4. **Engage Actively**: Ask questions or contribute to discussions to keep your mind engaged and prevent drifting off.\n\n5. **Limit Distractions**: If possible, choose a seat away from distractions and use noise-cancelling headphones or earplugs to minimize background noise.\n\n6. **Practice Mindfulness**: Techniques such as deep breathing can help ground you and refocus your attention when you feel distracted.\n\n7. **Request Shorter Meetings**: If possible, advocate for brief meetings, as shorter durations can help maintain your concentration.\n\nBy integrating these strategies, you can enhance your ability to stay attentive and participate effectively in meetings.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0019-85-03855:11": 1.2807468175888062,
            "clueweb22-en0008-61-11890:3": 0.0955476388335228
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      }
    ],
    "judgment": {
      "engagement": "Effective Collaborator",
      "relevance-and-usefulness": "Moderately Meets",
      "overall-subtopic-quality": "Acceptable",
      "subtopic-justification": "Using ear plugs and noise cancelling headphones",
      "rater-confidence": "High confidence"
    }
  },
  {
    "runtag": "genaius-full-rewrite",
    "type": "ikat-dialog-v1",
    "topic": "8-1",
    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2018m interested in ADHD management at work. What are some effective ways people manage it?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can ADHD be managed?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Managing ADHD at work often involves creating a structured environment and using strategies tailored to individual needs. For example, minimizing distractions by using headphones or working in quieter spaces can help with focus. Maintaining an organized workspace and keeping detailed notes can address forgetfulness and improve task management. Time management techniques, like avoiding over-scheduling and using tools such as calendars or timers, are also effective. Additionally, seeking support from ADHD coaches or joining support groups can provide personalized strategies and encouragement. Since you enjoy daydreaming, strategies to redirect focus, like the Pomodoro Technique, might be particularly helpful. Incorporating breaks and recovery activities, such as light exercise or creative outlets, can also combat fatigue and enhance productivity. These approaches can be adapted to fit your preferences and lifestyle, ensuring a more manageable and fulfilling work experience.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0025-75-16053:0": 15.55519962310791,
            "clueweb22-en0019-85-03855:10": 14.05210018157959,
            "clueweb22-en0036-02-14625:10": 13.594799995422363
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I often daydream.",
            "I sometimes suddenly feel tired.",
            "Sometimes I feel awkward when others are around.",
            "I have a sedentary lifestyle."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Is there a method to avoid feeling overwhelmed when switching between tasks?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to manage multiple tasks at work while having ADHD?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To avoid feeling overwhelmed when switching between tasks, breaking tasks into smaller, manageable steps can be very effective. This approach helps reduce the sense of being overwhelmed by large projects. For example, instead of thinking about completing an entire report, focus on writing just the introduction first. Additionally, using structured routines, such as scheduling specific blocks of time for tasks, can help create a sense of order and reduce anxiety. The Pomodoro Technique, where you work in focused intervals with short breaks, might also be helpful for maintaining energy and focus. Since you sometimes feel tired, incorporating brief, energizing activities like stretching or a quick walk between tasks can refresh your mind and body. Lastly, consider switching between two tasks throughout the day to maintain engagement and prevent burnout. This flexibility can make transitions feel less daunting and more natural.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0036-02-14625:4": 19.09269905090332,
            "clueweb22-en0007-85-19058:8": 18.576799392700195,
            "clueweb22-en0036-02-14625:3": 18.5585994720459
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I often daydream.",
            "I sometimes suddenly feel tired."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "How can a timer help people with ADHD to focus on a single task?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can a timer help people with ADHD to focus on a single task?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "A timer can be a powerful tool for people with ADHD to focus on a single task by providing structure and clear boundaries for work and breaks. The Pomodoro Technique is a popular method that uses a timer to create focused work intervals. You set the timer for 25 minutes and dedicate that time solely to one task, avoiding distractions. When the timer goes off, you take a short 5-minute break before starting another session. This approach helps maintain attention and prevents fatigue by breaking work into manageable chunks. For someone who enjoys daydreaming, the timer can act as a gentle reminder to stay on track, while the scheduled breaks allow space for mental relaxation. Over time, this method can improve focus and productivity, making transitions between tasks smoother and less overwhelming.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0001-66-11662:19": 31.002599716186523
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I often daydream.",
            "I sometimes suddenly feel tired."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "How can a person with ADHD handle distractions while in hyperfocus?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can a person with ADHD handle distractions while in hyperfocus?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Handling distractions during hyperfocus can be challenging for someone with ADHD, but there are strategies to manage it effectively. First, creating a distraction-free environment is key\u2014this might include using noise-canceling headphones or working in a quiet space. Setting clear goals for the task at hand can also help maintain focus, as it provides a roadmap for what needs to be accomplished. Additionally, incorporating feedback loops, such as checking progress at regular intervals, can help you stay on track without veering off into unrelated activities. Since hyperfocus often occurs on tasks that are personally meaningful or engaging, ensuring the task aligns with your interests can make it easier to sustain productive focus. Finally, using tools like timers or alarms can gently pull you out of hyperfocus when needed, allowing you to transition to other responsibilities without feeling overwhelmed. These strategies can help balance the benefits of hyperfocus while minimizing its potential downsides.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0027-21-04278:8": 24.636600494384766,
            "clueweb22-en0022-33-08001:0": 24.35300064086914,
            "clueweb22-en0016-28-02016:6": 22.75309944152832
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I often daydream.",
            "I like making up crazy stories for normal events."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "What if meetings are long and I start to zone out\u2014how do I stay attentive with ADHD?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to stay attentive in meetings while having ADHD?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Long meetings can be particularly challenging for someone with ADHD, especially if zoning out becomes an issue. To stay attentive, consider strategies like active engagement\u2014taking notes or asking questions can help keep your mind focused on the discussion. If possible, request an agenda beforehand to prepare and identify key points to concentrate on. Using a timer or setting reminders during the meeting can also help you refocus periodically. Since you enjoy daydreaming, incorporating brief mental resets, like doodling or jotting down ideas related to the meeting, might keep your mind engaged without drifting too far. Additionally, staying hydrated and taking short breaks, if allowed, can combat fatigue and improve alertness. If zoning out persists, you might explore mindfulness techniques or cognitive exercises to strengthen your ability to stay present during extended periods of focus. These strategies can be tailored to your needs, ensuring meetings feel more manageable and productive.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0001-45-03598:8": 16.93899917602539
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I often daydream.",
            "I sometimes suddenly feel tired."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thank you for sharing your insights and asking thoughtful questions! I hope these strategies help make your work experience more manageable and fulfilling. If you have more questions in the future, feel free to reach out. Take care and farewell!",
          "user_rubrik": null,
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": null,
          "citations": {},
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      }
    ],
