      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "What are some ways to make meetings less distracting for someone with ADHD?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to stay attentive in meetings while having ADHD?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To make meetings less distracting for someone with ADHD, you can try several strategies to maintain focus and minimize interruptions. First, keeping a notepad handy to jot down key points or ideas can help you stay engaged while also providing an outlet for restlessness. Second, using headphones to play white noise or calming music before the meeting can help reduce external distractions. Third, request a clear agenda in advance so you can prepare mentally and focus on the most relevant topics. Additionally, consider sitting in a spot with fewer visual distractions, such as away from windows or high-traffic areas. If possible, discuss accommodations with your team, like shorter, more focused meetings or breaks during longer sessions. These adjustments can help create a more ADHD-friendly meeting environment.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0019-85-03855:10": 26.223800659179688,
            "clueweb22-en0019-85-03855:11": 20.825300216674805,
            "clueweb22-en0025-75-16053:1": 20.11680030822754
          },
