  {
    "runtag": "genaius-summary-rewrite",
    "type": "ikat-fragment-v1",
    "topic": "8-1",
    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "How can a timer help people with ADHD to focus on a single task?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can a timer help people with ADHD to focus on a single task?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Using a timer can be an effective tool for individuals with ADHD to focus on a single task. Timers provide a clear, external structure that helps create a sense of urgency and accountability. For example, visual timers, which show the passage of time through disappearing colors or moving sand, can make time more tangible and easier to track. This can be particularly helpful for those who struggle with \"time blindness,\" a common ADHD challenge where time feels abstract.\n\nThe Pomodoro Technique is a popular method that involves setting a timer for 25 minutes of focused work, followed by a 5-minute break. This approach breaks tasks into manageable chunks, making it easier to maintain attention and avoid burnout. Additionally, timers can be paired with scheduled breaks to prevent fatigue and maintain productivity over longer periods.\n\nBy using a timer, you can also consciously limit the time spent on tasks you enjoy, preventing hyperfocus on one activity at the expense of others. Over time, this practice can help improve time management and task completion. Experiment with different types of timers\u2014whether visual, auditory, or app-based\u2014to find what works best for your needs.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0011-76-08014:5": 18.861600875854492,
            "clueweb22-en0026-06-01592:6": 18.62350082397461,
            "clueweb22-en0001-66-11662:18": 18.517900466918945
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      }
    ],
    "judgment": {
      "engagement": "True Collaborative Partner",
      "relevance-and-usefulness": "Highly meets",
      "overall-subtopic-quality": "Good",
      "subtopic-justification": "Visual timers were good given the PTKB this person likes art and draws.",
      "rater-confidence": "High confidence"
    }
  },
  {
    "runtag": "genaius-summary-rewrite",
    "type": "ikat-fragment-v1",
    "topic": "8-1",
    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "How can a person with ADHD handle distractions while in hyperfocus?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can a person with ADHD handle distractions while in hyperfocus?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Handling distractions during hyperfocus can be challenging, but there are strategies to help manage this. First, set up external reminders, like alarms or timers, to periodically check in with your surroundings. This can help you break out of hyperfocus when necessary. Second, create a structured environment by minimizing potential distractions beforehand\u2014this might include silencing notifications or using noise-canceling headphones. Third, establish clear priorities and goals for your task so you can redirect your focus if you veer off track. Finally, practice mindfulness techniques to increase awareness of when you\u2019re becoming overly absorbed in a task. These strategies can help you maintain balance and stay productive without losing track of other responsibilities.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0022-33-08001:0": 21.15530014038086,
            "clueweb22-en0014-54-13628:2": 20.630800247192383,
            "clueweb22-en0006-32-02164:17": 19.520999908447266
