  {
    "runtag": "grilllab-agentic-gpt4.1-larf-v2",
    "type": "ikat-dialog-v1",
    "topic": "8-1",
    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I'm looking into how ADHD can be managed, especially at work. What are some general ways people handle it?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can ADHD be managed?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "People with ADHD often handle workplace challenges by using strategies such as wearing headphones to reduce noise distractions, maintaining a clutter-free and organized workspace, and keeping notes to help with forgetfulness and restlessness. It's also helpful to avoid over-scheduling and to use computer aids for scheduling tasks. Some individuals benefit from requesting a quiet workspace or working during less busy hours. Many experts recommend self-accommodating\u2014making personal adjustments to your work environment\u2014rather than formally disclosing an ADHD diagnosis, as this can be more effective and less stressful in some workplaces. Seeking support from career counselors or mental health professionals can also help tailor strategies to your unique needs [DOC-1][DOC-2][DOC-4]. How can I talk to my employer about ADHD accommodations?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0019-85-03855:10": 0.07894223263075724,
            "clueweb22-en0025-75-16053:0": 0.07560535840105732,
            "clueweb22-en0019-85-03855:9": 0.055877754086709315,
            "clueweb22-en0041-27-15270:0": 0.05475026301424586
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I work in an office.",
            "I have a sedentary lifestyle.",
            "Sometimes I feel awkward when others are around.",
            "I sometimes suddenly feel tired."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That was helpful, thanks! Can you give tips for discussing ADHD and accommodations with a boss without making it awkward?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can ADHD be managed?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "You can request accommodations by focusing on your needs rather than your diagnosis, and by highlighting how changes will help your productivity, which can make the conversation less awkward. How does German law protect employees with ADHD?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0044-40-11164:4": 0.07634769991659812,
            "clueweb22-en0033-18-04361:17": 0.07119699797449158,
            "clueweb22-en0044-40-11164:3": 0.07112302403120499,
            "clueweb22-en0026-09-15240:12": 0.06995228877119444
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "Sometimes I feel awkward when others are around.",
            "I work in an office.",
            "I live in Germany."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s helpful, thanks! What rights do I have in Germany if I need adjustments at my workplace because of ADHD?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can ADHD be managed?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "If ADHD substantially limits your ability to perform your job, you may be protected under German disability law (Schwerbehindertenrecht), which requires employers to provide reasonable accommodations to help you succeed at work. These adjustments can include changes to your workspace, flexible hours, or additional breaks. To access these rights, you typically need a formal diagnosis and, in some cases, official recognition of your disability status (Schwerbehindertenausweis). You are not required to disclose your diagnosis unless you seek formal accommodations, and you can discuss your needs with your employer or HR without sharing specific medical details. If you face discrimination or difficulty obtaining accommodations, you can seek advice from legal advocates or disability rights organizations in Germany. It's important to know your rights and, if needed, consult with a legal expert familiar with German disability law to ensure you receive appropriate support [DOC-1][DOC-2][DOC-4]. Are there organizations in Germany that support employees with ADHD?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0030-27-00075:2": 0.06350006400409626,
            "clueweb22-en0030-27-00075:1": 0.0620789364169239,
            "clueweb22-en0030-27-00075:0": 0.05988527601430828,
            "clueweb22-en0038-52-05284:13": 0.049646310645294234
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I live in Germany.",
            "I work in an office."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Do you know of any groups or local resources here in Germany that support office workers dealing with ADHD?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to manage multiple tasks at work while having ADHD?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "For office workers in Germany dealing with ADHD, there are several resources available. ADHS Deutschland e.V. is a prominent organization that provides information, support groups, and advocacy for adults with ADHD. They have local chapters (Ortsgruppen) in many cities, where you can connect with others facing similar challenges. Additionally, many cities have Selbsthilfegruppen (self-help groups) specifically for adults or working professionals with ADHD\u2014these can be found via local health offices or online directories. Therapists specializing in ADHD and workplace coaching are also available; you can ask your general practitioner or local mental health clinic for referrals. Online communities and podcasts, such as those discussed in German media, can also offer support and practical advice for managing ADHD at work [DOC-1][DOC-5]. Would you like help finding a local ADHD support group in your city?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0043-57-05105:6": 0.03028233151183971,
            "clueweb22-en0019-81-12016:9": 0.028790389395194696,
            "clueweb22-en0023-71-15878:3": 0.02844551282051282,
