            "clueweb22-en0035-93-06191:21": 0.026540946394272742
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I live in Germany.",
            "I work in an office."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "No, that\u2019s okay. I like reading about it on my own first.  \nCould you give specific strategies for juggling multiple tasks at work with ADHD? That would help.",
          "user_rubrik": "How to manage multiple tasks at work while having ADHD?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Managing multiple tasks at work with ADHD can be made easier by using digital tools like calendar apps with alerts to keep track of appointments and deadlines, and by breaking larger projects into smaller, manageable steps to reduce overwhelm. Setting timers can help prevent hyperfocus on one task and ensure you switch between responsibilities as needed. Prioritizing tasks with a clear, written to-do list\u2014either on paper or digitally\u2014can help you focus on what's most important and avoid procrastination. Some people also benefit from working with an ADHD coach, who can provide accountability and help develop personalized strategies for organization, planning, and stress management. Using headphones to block out distractions and keeping your workspace organized are also effective ways to stay on track in an office environment [clueweb22-en0036-02-14625:2][clueweb22-en0029-54-11499:0][clueweb22-en0033-15-10365:0][clueweb22-en0019-85-03855:9]. Are you interested in learning more about ADHD coaching?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0019-85-03855:9": 0.042844410491469316,
            "clueweb22-en0036-02-14625:2": 0.04098238205738529,
            "clueweb22-en0029-54-11499:0": 0.03834896810506566,
            "clueweb22-en0033-15-10365:0": 0.03263183606304476
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I work in an office.",
            "I have a sedentary lifestyle.",
            "I love it when it is quiet."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Maybe later!  \nHow can a timer help people with ADHD to focus on a single task?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can a timer help people with ADHD to focus on a single task?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "Using a timer can help people with ADHD focus on a single task by providing a visual or auditory cue that marks the beginning and end of a work period. Techniques like the Pomodoro method\u2014working for 25 minutes, then taking a 5-minute break\u2014use timers to break work into manageable chunks, which can boost motivation and reduce overwhelm [clueweb22-en0012-51-00120:12]. Timers also help prevent hyperfocus, reminding you to pause and switch tasks or take care of basic needs like eating [clueweb22-en0012-51-00120:12]. Specialized timers, such as those with visual countdowns or vibrating alerts, can be especially helpful for people who lose track of time easily [clueweb22-en0007-41-01613:0]. What timer apps or devices are recommended for ADHD?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0007-41-01613:0": 0.04152811606480991,
