  {
    "runtag": "grilllab-agentic-gpt4.1-larf-v2",
    "type": "ikat-fragment-v1",
    "topic": "8-1",
    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I'm looking into how ADHD can be managed, especially at work. What are some general ways people handle it?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can ADHD be managed?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "People with ADHD often handle workplace challenges by using strategies such as wearing headphones to reduce noise distractions, maintaining a clutter-free and organized workspace, and keeping notes to help with forgetfulness and restlessness. It's also helpful to avoid over-scheduling and to use computer aids for scheduling tasks. Some individuals benefit from requesting a quiet workspace or working during less busy hours. Many experts recommend self-accommodating\u2014making personal adjustments to your work environment\u2014rather than formally disclosing an ADHD diagnosis, as this can be more effective and less stressful in some workplaces. Seeking support from career counselors or mental health professionals can also help tailor strategies to your unique needs [DOC-1][DOC-2][DOC-4]. How can I talk to my employer about ADHD accommodations?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0019-85-03855:10": 0.07894223263075724,
            "clueweb22-en0025-75-16053:0": 0.07560535840105732,
            "clueweb22-en0019-85-03855:9": 0.055877754086709315,
            "clueweb22-en0041-27-15270:0": 0.05475026301424586
