            "I work in an office.",
            "I live in Germany."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s helpful, thanks! What rights do I have in Germany if I need adjustments at my workplace because of ADHD?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can ADHD be managed?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "If ADHD substantially limits your ability to perform your job, you may be protected under German disability law (Schwerbehindertenrecht), which requires employers to provide reasonable accommodations to help you succeed at work. These adjustments can include changes to your workspace, flexible hours, or additional breaks. To access these rights, you typically need a formal diagnosis and, in some cases, official recognition of your disability status (Schwerbehindertenausweis). You are not required to disclose your diagnosis unless you seek formal accommodations, and you can discuss your needs with your employer or HR without sharing specific medical details. If you face discrimination or difficulty obtaining accommodations, you can seek advice from legal advocates or disability rights organizations in Germany. It's important to know your rights and, if needed, consult with a legal expert familiar with German disability law to ensure you receive appropriate support [DOC-1][DOC-2][DOC-4]. Are there organizations in Germany that support employees with ADHD?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0030-27-00075:2": 0.06350006400409626,
            "clueweb22-en0030-27-00075:1": 0.0620789364169239,
            "clueweb22-en0030-27-00075:0": 0.05988527601430828,
