      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "No, that\u2019s okay. I like reading about it on my own first.  \nCould you give specific strategies for juggling multiple tasks at work with ADHD? That would help.",
          "user_rubrik": "How to manage multiple tasks at work while having ADHD?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Managing multiple tasks at work with ADHD can be made easier by using digital tools like calendar apps with alerts to keep track of appointments and deadlines, and by breaking larger projects into smaller, manageable steps to reduce overwhelm. Setting timers can help prevent hyperfocus on one task and ensure you switch between responsibilities as needed. Prioritizing tasks with a clear, written to-do list\u2014either on paper or digitally\u2014can help you focus on what's most important and avoid procrastination. Some people also benefit from working with an ADHD coach, who can provide accountability and help develop personalized strategies for organization, planning, and stress management. Using headphones to block out distractions and keeping your workspace organized are also effective ways to stay on track in an office environment [clueweb22-en0036-02-14625:2][clueweb22-en0029-54-11499:0][clueweb22-en0033-15-10365:0][clueweb22-en0019-85-03855:9]. Are you interested in learning more about ADHD coaching?",
