      {
        "turn": 8,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Yeah, I\u2019m interested! What are other tools aside from timers that can help with focus and organization at work?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can a timer help people with ADHD to focus on a single task?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "Beyond timers, many adults with ADHD find digital to-do list apps like Evernote and Priority Matrix useful for capturing ideas, organizing tasks, and setting reminders [clueweb22-en0040-16-00993:1]. Project management tools such as Asana help break down projects into manageable steps and track progress [clueweb22-en0032-38-16716:0]. Fidget tools or small objects to keep your hands busy can improve focus during meetings or long work sessions [clueweb22-en0005-70-11136:3]. White noise machines or apps can help create a quiet environment, which is especially valuable if you love it when it is quiet and work in a shared office [clueweb22-en0032-38-16716:0]. Many people also use calendar apps with customizable alerts to manage appointments and deadlines, and some prefer physical tools like sticky notes or color-coded notebooks for visual organization [clueweb22-en0005-70-11136:2].",
