      {
        "turn": 9,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "This is great\u2014thank you!  \nWhat about when someone with ADHD is in hyperfocus? How can they handle distractions then, especially in an office?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can a person with ADHD handle distractions while in hyperfocus?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Managing hyperfocus in an office setting involves setting clear boundaries before starting a task\u2014decide in advance how long you'll spend on it and use timers or alarms to signal when it's time to switch activities. Highly visible reminders, such as sticky notes or digital alerts, can help break your focus when necessary. If timers alone aren't enough, enlisting a coworker or accountability partner to check in or send a message can be effective. Mindfulness exercises and physically changing your position (like standing up or stretching) can also help you become aware of time passing and transition out of hyperfocus. These strategies not only help manage distractions but also allow you to harness the benefits of hyperfocus for productivity while maintaining balance in your workday [clueweb22-en0013-60-10409:7][clueweb22-en0007-71-00778:7][clueweb22-en0012-74-13153:5][clueweb22-en0012-74-13153:6]. Are there specific distractions you struggle with most during hyperfocus?",
