          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For managing tasks with ADHD, Evernote is highly recommended for organizing to-dos, handwritten notes, reminders, and even educational content, making it easier to keep track of tasks and ideas in one place [DOC-1]. Google Calendar is another excellent tool for scheduling appointments, setting reminders, and planning focused work blocks, which can help you stay on top of deadlines and structure your day [DOC-2]. Procraster (iOS only) is specifically designed to help users identify and overcome procrastination triggers, making it easier to start and complete tasks [DOC-3]. These apps are praised for their ability to provide structure, reminders, and accountability, which are especially helpful for office workers with ADHD. Are you interested in non-digital tools or physical planners for ADHD?",
