          "user_rubrik": "How can a person with ADHD handle distractions while in hyperfocus?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Managing distractions while in hyperfocus with ADHD involves several strategies. Before starting a task, decide on a reasonable time commitment and set boundaries for how long you'll work. Use multiple highly visible reminders, such as alarms, timers, or sticky notes, to prompt you to check in with yourself or take breaks. Involving colleagues or friends\u2014by asking them to send a message or give you a gentle nudge at set times\u2014can also help you break free from hyperfocus when necessary. Practicing mindfulness and moving around when you realize you're in hyperfocus can further help you regain awareness and control. These techniques not only help manage distractions but also allow you to harness hyperfocus as a productive asset when balanced with regular check-ins and breaks [clueweb22-en0007-71-00778][clueweb22-en0012-74-13153]. Would you like tips for setting up effective reminders or alarms?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0007-71-00778:7": 0.04550236900780379,
            "clueweb22-en0006-62-03234:3": 0.04504312675751676,
