      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Actually, I\u2019d like to know how to stay attentive in meetings while having ADHD. Any practical advice?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to stay attentive in meetings while having ADHD?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Practical strategies for staying attentive in meetings with ADHD include keeping a notepad to jot down key points or doodle, which can help channel restlessness and maintain focus [clueweb22-en0019-85-03855][clueweb22-en0032-22-09151]. Using discreet fidget tools, such as stress balls or fidget rings, can also help manage excess energy without drawing attention [clueweb22-en0036-02-14625]. If you find it difficult to sit still, consider requesting short breaks or the option to stand or move during longer meetings\u2014many workplaces are open to such reasonable adjustments [clueweb22-en0018-75-17093]. Creating a distraction-free environment, like sitting away from doors or windows, and using headphones before meetings to calm your mind, can further support your focus. Are you interested in digital tools for capturing meeting notes?",
          "citations": {
