    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m looking for ways ADHD can be managed, especially at work. Any ideas?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can ADHD be managed?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 4,
          "text": "Managing ADHD in the workplace often involves a combination of environmental adjustments and personal strategies. For those who value quiet, requesting a private office, quiet cubicle, or using unused spaces like conference rooms can help reduce external distractions. Headphones with white noise or soothing music are also effective for blocking out background noise. Organizational tools such as notepads for jotting down ideas, keeping a clutter-free workspace, and using computer aids for scheduling can help manage forgetfulness and improve focus. It's also helpful to route calls to voicemail and respond at set times, and to avoid over-scheduling to prevent time management issues. If needed, reasonable accommodations like extra time to complete tasks or written instructions can be requested. These strategies are especially relevant for office workers with a sedentary lifestyle who value a quiet environment and may experience distractibility or daydreaming at work [DOC-1][DOC-2][DOC-3][DOC-4]. Would you like specific organizational tools or apps recommended for ADHD?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0025-75-16053:0": 0.07506891425616893,
