    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Actually, I\u2019m curious about timers\u2014how can using a timer help someone with ADHD focus on a single task?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can a timer help people with ADHD to focus on a single task?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Timers, such as those used in the Pomodoro Technique (working in 25-minute intervals with breaks), provide both visual and audible prompts that help individuals with ADHD stay on task by breaking work into manageable chunks and signaling when to start or stop [clueweb22-en0033-18-04361][clueweb22-en0038-91-03346]. This method creates a sense of urgency, making it easier to focus on a single task and reducing the temptation to multitask or become distracted. Timers can also be used to schedule breaks, which are important for maintaining focus and preventing fatigue. Consistent use of timers helps reinforce time management and pacing, making it easier to transition between tasks and stay organized [clueweb22-en0026-62-07087]. Would you like recommendations for specific timer apps or devices?",
