          "user_rubrik": "How to manage multiple tasks at work while having ADHD?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For adults with ADHD, digital tools like Google Calendar are highly recommended for scheduling appointments, setting reminders, and blocking out focused work time [clueweb22-en0006-19-19181:13]. Task management apps such as Trello and Todoist help break down projects into smaller, manageable steps and keep track of progress [clueweb22-en0033-18-04361:4]. The Pomodoro Technique, which involves working in short intervals with breaks, can be implemented using various timer apps or browser-based tools like Tomato Timer [clueweb22-en0033-18-04361:4]. Some people also find paper planners, bullet journals, or notepads helpful for visualizing tasks and maintaining consistency [clueweb22-en0029-26-11797:4]. Experimenting with these tools and sticking with one that fits your style can make managing multiple tasks much easier. Do you prefer digital or paper-based organization tools?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0006-19-19181:13": 0.05503326330532213,
            "clueweb22-en0029-26-11797:4": 0.050438419270147083,
