    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I actually prefer digital tools\u2014my workspace is tidy and I like things uncluttered. How can a timer help people with ADHD to focus on a single task?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can a timer help people with ADHD to focus on a single task?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Using a timer\u2014such as a digital app or a physical device\u2014can be especially effective for adults with ADHD because it creates external structure and helps manage time blindness, a common challenge with ADHD. Techniques like the Pomodoro Technique involve setting a timer for 25 minutes of focused work followed by a short break, which can make large tasks feel less overwhelming and help maintain attention [clueweb22-en0026-06-01592:6]. Visual timers, which show the passage of time with a colored disk or countdown, provide a constant, non-intrusive reminder to stay on task [clueweb22-en0007-41-01613:0]. Many timer apps are available for smartphones and computers, allowing you to customize intervals and receive alerts or vibrations, which can be especially helpful in a quiet, uncluttered workspace [clueweb22-en0016-80-03538:5]. Would you like recommendations for specific timer apps for ADHD?",
