    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Maybe later! About hyperfocus\u2014how can someone with ADHD deal with distractions if they\u2019re stuck in hyperfocus mode?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can a person with ADHD handle distractions while in hyperfocus?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "When someone with ADHD is in hyperfocus, it can be difficult to shift attention away from a task, even when it's necessary. Effective strategies include setting multiple highly visible reminders\u2014such as alarms, digital timers, or pop-up notifications\u2014to prompt you to check the time or switch tasks [clueweb22-en0012-74-13153:6][clueweb22-en0013-60-10409:7]. Enlisting a trusted colleague or friend to send a message or give a gentle nudge at a set time can also help break the spell of hyperfocus. Practicing mindfulness and being aware of your tendency to hyperfocus can make it easier to catch yourself and transition out of it. Physically moving\u2014like standing up or changing your position\u2014can also help you reset your attention [clueweb22-en0007-71-00778:7]. Setting clear goals and taking breaks when you reach them is another way to manage hyperfocus productively. Are you interested in mindfulness exercises for attention management?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0003-10-11901:10": 0.07917200590554636,
