      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I'm looking for information on how ADHD can be managed. What can you tell me?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can ADHD be managed?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "ADHD management is highly individualized but centers on a combination of behavioral strategies, education, and\u2014when appropriate\u2014medication. Here\u2019s what works best, based on age and evidence:\n\n**Core Management Strategies**\n- **Behavioral Therapy:** First-line for young children (ages 4\u20135); also recommended for older children and adults, often combined with other treatments. Includes parent/teacher training, skills coaching, and cognitive behavioral therapy.\n- **Medication:** Stimulants (like methylphenidate and amphetamines) are most effective for ages 6\u201318 and adults. Non-stimulant options (e.g., atomoxetine, modafinil) exist for those who don\u2019t tolerate stimulants.\n- **Education & Skills Training:** For parents, children, and adults\u2014focuses on understanding ADHD, building routines, and improving organization and social skills.\n- **School/Work Accommodations:** Collaboration with teachers or employers to create supportive environments is crucial.\n\n**Additional Supports**\n- **Lifestyle Adjustments:** Regular sleep, structured routines, and sometimes tools like weighted blankets or music",
          "citations": {
