      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That makes sense! What are some common distractions in an office that people with ADHD should be aware of?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to stay attentive in meetings while having ADHD?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "For adults with ADHD in an office, the most common distractions\u2014and the ones that most undermine focus\u2014are:\n\n**1. Visual Clutter**\n- Messy desks, piles of paper, and scattered objects create constant visual reminders of unfinished tasks, making it harder to concentrate (clueweb22-en0023-24-19944, clueweb22-en0012-95-11946).\n\n**2. Noise and Interruptions**\n- Background chatter, ringing phones, and colleagues dropping by are especially disruptive for ADHD brains, which are more sensitive to external stimuli (clueweb22-en0019-85-03855, clueweb22-en0006-74-15539).\n\n**3. Digital Distractions**\n- Frequent email notifications, chat messages, and social media alerts fragment attention and make it difficult to return to deep work (clueweb22-en0030-54-18668, clueweb22-en0006-74-15539).\n\n**4. Internal Distractions**\n- Mind-wandering, overthinking, and anxiety about unfinished tasks or upcoming meetings can pull",
