          "user_rubrik": "How to stay attentive in meetings while having ADHD?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To create a more focused workspace for ADHD in an office\u2014especially given your tendency to daydream and a sedentary lifestyle\u2014prioritize these evidence-backed adjustments:\n\n**1. Declutter Ruthlessly**\n- Keep only essentials on your desk; visual clutter (papers, mugs, random objects) subconsciously distracts and increases daydreaming (clueweb22-en0023-24-19944, clueweb22-en0030-09-07150).\n- Schedule regular (daily/weekly) desk cleanups to maintain order.\n\n**2. Control Noise and Interruptions**\n- Use noise-cancelling headphones or play white noise/classical music to block office chatter and sudden sounds (clueweb22-en0019-85-03855, clueweb22-en0025-75-16053).\n- If possible, request a quieter workspace or use unused rooms for deep work.\n\n**3. Minimize Digital Distractions**\n- Silence phone and computer notifications; batch-check emails and messages at set times (clueweb22-en0029-09-07368, clueweb",
