      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That sounds helpful! What specific strategies work best for managing multiple tasks at work?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to manage multiple tasks at work while having ADHD?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To manage multiple tasks at work with ADHD, focus on strategies tailored to how your brain works\u2014not generic productivity tips. Here\u2019s what\u2019s most effective for office environments:\n\n**1. Task Management & Prioritization**\n- Break large projects into small, actionable steps. Use checklists or digital task managers.\n- Prioritize tasks visually (color-coding, sticky notes, or apps) to clarify what\u2019s urgent vs. important.\n- Use \u201cbrain dumps\u201d to clear your mind, then organize tasks by priority.\n\n**2. Time Management**\n- Use structured techniques like the Pomodoro Method (work in short, timed bursts with breaks).\n- Set timers or alarms for task switching and deadlines.\n- Schedule focused work blocks for high-priority tasks, minimizing interruptions.\n\n**3. Organization & Environment**\n- Keep your workspace clutter-free to reduce distractions.\n- Use visual cues (whiteboards, calendars) to track progress and deadlines.\n- Limit digital distractions\u2014close unused tabs, silence notifications.\n\n**4. Accountability & Support**\n- Consider an ADHD coach or CBT therapist for personalized strategies and regular check-ins",
