          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Great insights! How does a timer specifically enhance focus for someone with ADHD?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can a timer help people with ADHD to focus on a single task?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "A timer is a powerful focus tool for ADHD in an office setting because it provides external structure and immediate feedback\u2014two things the ADHD brain craves but struggles to self-generate.\n\n**How Timers Enhance Focus for ADHD:**\n\n- **Creates Urgency & Boundaries:** A visible or audible countdown (like a Pomodoro timer) signals a clear start and stop, making it easier to resist distractions and stay on task (clueweb22-en0038-91-03346, clueweb22-en0011-76-08014).\n- **Breaks Work Into Manageable Chunks:** Short, timed work sessions (typically 25 minutes) followed by breaks prevent overwhelm and mental fatigue, helping you sustain attention throughout the day (clueweb22-en0011-52-17888, clueweb22-en0013-76-05533).\n- **Reduces Time Blindness:** Timers make the passage of time visible, counteracting the ADHD tendency to lose track of time and miss deadlines (clueweb22-en0007-41-01613, clueweb",
          "citations": {
