      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m curious about ways to manage ADHD at work. What kind of strategies are there?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can ADHD be managed?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "There are several strategies to manage ADHD at work. These include using organizational tools such as planners, timers, and apps to stay on track and meet deadlines. Breaking down large tasks into smaller, manageable chunks can also help. Additionally, creating a quiet and distraction-free workspace, taking regular breaks, and prioritizing tasks can be beneficial. Some people also find it helpful to use the Pomodoro Technique, which involves working in focused 25-minute increments, followed by a 5-minute break. It's also important to communicate with your employer and colleagues about your needs and challenges, and to explore possible accommodations, such as flexible work arrangements or the use of assistive technology. By implementing these strategies, individuals with ADHD can better manage their symptoms and improve their productivity at work.  Consider seeking guidance from a professional, such as a therapist or coach, who can help you develop a personalized plan to manage your ADHD at work.",
          "citations": {
