  {
    "runtag": "orga-llama70b-bm25-minilm-llama70b",
    "type": "ikat-dialog-v1",
    "topic": "8-1",
    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m looking for ways to manage ADHD at work. What are some strategies people use?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can ADHD be managed?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "You can try using \"white noise\" earphones or listening to classical music to drown out office noises. Alternatively, you can request a private office or quiet cubicle, or work from home when possible. If that's not feasible, you can also try working in an unused space,",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0025-75-16053:1": 5.213716506958008,
            "clueweb22-en0019-85-03855:10": 4.734659194946289,
            "clueweb22-en0009-70-10081:11": 2.8852415084838867,
            "clueweb22-en0025-75-16053:0": 2.739487648010254,
            "clueweb22-en0029-78-02009:6": 2.45644211769104
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, but that's not quite what I meant. Can you share broader management strategies for ADHD, maybe more general tips, not just about noise?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can ADHD be managed?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To manage ADHD at work, consider using a planner or calendar to stay organized and on track. Breaking down tasks into smaller, manageable chunks can also help. Additionally, setting clear goals and priorities can aid in maintaining focus. Establishing a daily routine and sticking to it can provide a sense of structure and help minimize distractions. It's also essential to take regular breaks to recharge and avoid burnout. By implementing these strategies, you can better manage your ADHD symptoms and improve your overall productivity at work.  Regular exercise and healthy eating can also help alleviate ADHD symptoms.  Maintaining a consistent sleep schedule is also crucial.  Building a support system, such as sharing your struggles with a trusted colleague or supervisor, can also provide valuable guidance and accommodations.  Using notes and to-do lists can help with forgetfulness and staying on top of tasks.  Avoiding over-scheduling and leaving some buffer time in your daily planner can help with time management.  Creating a clutter-free workspace can also help reduce distractions",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0019-85-03855:10": 3.5786588191986084,
            "clueweb22-en0002-73-18581:0": 1.8773261308670044,
            "clueweb22-en0032-22-09151:15": 1.8749275207519531,
            "clueweb22-en0008-79-03771:5": 1.4383933544158936,
            "clueweb22-en0009-70-10081:11": 1.2276033163070679
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Those sound useful! But what are some good ways to tackle multiple tasks at once without feeling overwhelmed, especially when distractions and tiredness make it hard to finish things?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to manage multiple tasks at work while having ADHD?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To tackle multiple tasks without feeling overwhelmed, try prioritizing them based on importance and deadlines. Focus on one task at a time, and use a timer to work in focused intervals, followed by a short break. This technique can help you stay on track and avoid burnout. Additionally, consider using a task list or calendar to keep track of your tasks and deadlines, and break down larger tasks into smaller, manageable chunks. Taking regular breaks to recharge and avoiding multitasking can also help you stay focused and productive, even when feeling tired or distracted. By implementing these strategies, you can better manage multiple tasks and maintain your productivity.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0032-31-16603:15": 3.378387212753296,
            "clueweb22-en0039-79-02293:3": 2.3126187324523926,
            "clueweb22-en0000-29-12469:4": 2.1775238513946533,
            "clueweb22-en0043-25-13249:11": 2.0418033599853516,
            "clueweb22-en0019-38-18911:15": 2.017617702484131
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "How can a timer actually help someone with ADHD focus better? Like, is there a special method or is it just about keeping track of time?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can a timer help people with ADHD to focus on a single task?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "A timer can help someone with ADHD focus better by providing a clear and structured work period, followed by a break. This technique is often referred to as the Pomodoro Technique, where you work in focused 25-minute intervals, followed by a 5-minute break. The timer helps to minimize distractions, stay on track, and maintain motivation. By using a timer, you can create a sense of urgency and help your brain stay focused on the task at hand, making it easier to complete tasks and avoid procrastination. This method can be especially helpful for individuals with ADHD, as it provides a clear and predictable structure, allowing them to better manage their time and attention.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0011-76-08014:6": 3.931441307067871,
            "clueweb22-en0027-64-05737:6": 3.6396801471710205,
            "clueweb22-en0034-10-07727:13": 2.638702869415283,
            "clueweb22-en0033-18-04361:4": 2.2225091457366943,
            "clueweb22-en0044-86-02193:1": 2.154754638671875
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Makes sense! Sometimes I find myself stuck in hyperfocus, though\u2014do you know ways someone with ADHD can handle unexpected distractions when they're really locked in on one thing?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can a person with ADHD handle distractions while in hyperfocus?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "When you're in a state of hyperfocus, it can be challenging to handle unexpected distractions. One strategy is to set a \"distraction protocol\" in advance, where you identify potential distractions and plan how to handle them. For example, you could set your phone to \"do not disturb\" mode or ask a colleague to handle interruptions. Another approach is to use a \"parking lot\" technique, where you quickly jot down the distraction and then refocus on your task, coming back to the distraction later. This can help you maintain your hyperfocus while still acknowledging the distraction. By having a plan in place, you can minimize the impact of distractions and stay focused on your task.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0036-30-15322:2": 4.105654239654541,
            "clueweb22-en0006-33-01092:4": 2.871027708053589,
            "clueweb22-en0006-33-01092:3": 2.551417827606201,
            "clueweb22-en0017-98-03504:9": 2.3743629455566406,
            "clueweb22-en0022-33-08001:0": 1.9569215774536133
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Interesting! What about meetings, though? How can I stay attentive in meetings when my mind starts to wander or I feel tired all of a sudden?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to stay attentive in meetings while having ADHD?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To stay attentive in meetings, try to sit near the front and maintain eye contact with the speaker. Taking notes can also help you stay engaged and focused. If you find your mind wandering, try to refocus on the conversation by summarizing what the speaker is saying in your own words. Additionally, consider discussing your ADHD with your colleagues or supervisor, so they can provide accommodations, such as providing meeting materials in advance or allowing you to take breaks during long meetings. This can help you stay attentive and participate more effectively in meetings. Regular exercise, healthy eating, and sufficient sleep can also help reduce fatigue and improve your ability to stay focused during meetings.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0028-52-02769:0": 2.5974667072296143,
            "clueweb22-en0045-43-06842:6": 2.016793966293335,
            "clueweb22-en0016-82-14243:26": 1.3640565872192383,
            "clueweb22-en0016-82-14243:25": 1.0011991262435913,
            "clueweb22-en0032-55-19547:2": 0.6376115083694458
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thank you so much for all your thoughtful suggestions and insights! You've really helped gather a comprehensive set of strategies for managing ADHD at work. I appreciate your time and input. Wishing you all the best\u2014farewell!",
          "user_rubrik": null,
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": null,
          "citations": {},
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      }
    ],
