          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s better, thanks! Are there any digital tools or apps that help with ADHD management at work?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can ADHD be managed?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 4,
          "text": "Yes, there are many digital tools and apps that can help with ADHD management at work. For example, apps like Wunderlist can help with organization and task management, while digital personal assistants like Siri or Alexa can help with reminders and calendar organization. Additionally, mindfulness apps like Headspace or Insight Timer can help with stress management and focus. These tools can be especially helpful for individuals with ADHD who struggle with executive function skills. They can also be used in conjunction with other strategies, such as breaking tasks into smaller steps and using a planner or calendar to stay organized. By using these digital tools and apps, individuals with ADHD can better manage their symptoms and be more productive at work. Get some exercise, like going for a walk during your lunch break, to help manage your ADHD symptoms. Exercise can help improve focus and reduce stress. Consider using a digital assistant, like Siri or Alexa, to help with reminders and calendar organization. These tools can be especially helpful for individuals with ADHD who struggle with executive function",
          "citations": {
