      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s super helpful! I get tired just sitting all day\u2014are there any tips for managing tiredness or sudden fatigue with ADHD at work?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to manage multiple tasks at work while having ADHD?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "Yes, managing tiredness or sudden fatigue with ADHD at work can be challenging. One strategy is to take regular breaks to stretch and move around. This can help increase energy levels and reduce fatigue. Additionally, prioritizing tasks and breaking them down into smaller, more manageable steps can help reduce feelings of overwhelm and fatigue. It may also be helpful to discuss your fatigue with your employer or HR manager to see if there are any accommodations that can be made, such as working part-time or having a flexible schedule. Getting enough sleep and practicing good sleep hygiene can also help reduce fatigue. Finally, using a planner or calendar to stay organized and on track can help reduce feelings of stress and fatigue. Consider talking to your doctor or a therapist about your fatigue, as they can help you develop a plan to manage it. They may also be able to recommend additional strategies or resources to help you cope with your ADHD symptoms. You can also try to find a quiet workspace or use noise-cancelling headphones to help you",
          "citations": {
