      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Interesting! How can a timer help people with ADHD to focus on a single task?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can a timer help people with ADHD to focus on a single task?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Using a timer can be a helpful strategy for individuals with ADHD to stay focused on a single task. By setting a timer for a specific amount of time, you can create a sense of urgency and help yourself stay on track. This can be especially helpful for tasks that you find boring or difficult to stay focused on. For example, you can set a timer for 25 minutes and work on a task without any distractions during that time. When the timer goes off, you can take a short break before returning to the task. This technique can help you stay focused and avoid getting sidetracked by distractions. Additionally, using a timer can help you develop a sense of self-discipline and responsibility, which can be beneficial for individuals with ADHD. It can also help you break down larger tasks into smaller, more manageable chunks, making it easier to stay focused and avoid feeling overwhelmed. By using a timer, you can create a sense of structure and routine, which can be helpful for individuals with ADHD who often",
