          "text": "When you're in a state of hyperfocus, it can be challenging to notice distractions around you. However, it's essential to be aware of your surroundings and take breaks to avoid burnout. One strategy is to set a timer for a specific amount of time, say 25 minutes, and work on your task without any distractions during that time. When the timer goes off, take a short break to stretch, move around, and refresh your mind. This can help you stay focused and avoid getting sidetracked by distractions. Additionally, consider using a tool or app that helps you stay organized and on track, such as a planner or a task management app. These tools can help you prioritize your tasks and avoid multitasking, which can be detrimental to your productivity. By being mindful of your surroundings and taking regular breaks, you can maintain your focus and make the most of your hyperfocus state. It's also essential to recognize when you're getting too engrossed in a task and need to",
