          "user_rubrik": "How to stay attentive in meetings while having ADHD?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Yes, staying attentive in long meetings can be challenging for individuals with ADHD. One strategy is to use a technique called \"active listening,\" where you focus on the speaker and try to understand the main points being discussed. You can also take notes or use a digital tool to help you stay organized and on track. Additionally, consider using a \"parking lot\" technique, where you write down any ideas or questions that come up during the meeting and deal with them later. This can help you stay focused on the current discussion and avoid getting sidetracked. It may also be helpful to discuss your meeting management strategies with your employer or HR manager to see if there are any accommodations that can be made, such as providing a quiet workspace or allowing you to take breaks during the meeting. Finally, consider using a mindfulness app or technique to help you stay focused and attentive during the meeting. By being proactive and using these strategies, you can stay attentive and engaged in long meetings, even with ADHD. Get enough",
