          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that's more relevant. How can a timer help people with ADHD to focus on a single task? Looking for specific examples.",
          "user_rubrik": "How can a timer help people with ADHD to focus on a single task?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "A timer can help individuals with ADHD focus on a single task by creating a sense of urgency and structure. For example, setting a 25-minute timer and challenging yourself to complete a task during that time can boost focus. When the timer goes off, take a short break before starting the next task. This technique, known as the Pomodoro Technique, can help you stay on track and avoid distractions. You can also use a timer to allocate specific times for tasks, helping you prioritize and manage your time more effectively. This can be especially helpful in a quiet workspace, which you prefer. By using a timer, you can create a productive routine and stay focused on your tasks.   However, I will revise the response to make it 170 words or less: A timer can help individuals with ADHD focus on a single task by creating a sense of urgency and structure. Setting a 25-minute timer and challenging yourself to complete a task during that time can boost focus. When the timer goes off,",
