      },
      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Good ideas, thank you! I actually like it to be quiet, so I\u2019ll skip the music. Are there ways to avoid feeling overwhelmed when juggling too many tasks?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to manage multiple tasks at work while having ADHD?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To avoid feeling overwhelmed when juggling tasks with ADHD, focus on one task at a time and break down large projects into smaller, manageable steps. Consider scheduling specific tasks rather than relying on general to-do lists, which can feel less daunting. Utilize techniques like the Pomodoro Method for focused work intervals. Also, learn to set boundaries, say no to new commitments if needed, and delegate tasks to colleagues to manage your workload effectively. Taking regular breaks and maintaining an organized workspace can also help.",
          "citations": {
