      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I see! When I\u2019m in hyperfocus, it\u2019s sometimes hard to notice time or distractions at all. How can someone with ADHD handle distractions during hyperfocus phases?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can a person with ADHD handle distractions while in hyperfocus?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To manage distractions during hyperfocus, especially when time awareness is lost, set multiple, highly visible reminders like loud alarms or timers that require physical interaction to turn off. You can also enlist a trusted person, such as a colleague or loved one, to gently interrupt you with a pre-arranged signal, message, or knock at specific times. Setting clear time boundaries for tasks before you start can also help prevent getting lost in hyperfocus.",
          "citations": {
