      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I like the Pomodoro idea\u2014how does a timer actually help someone with ADHD focus on a single task?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can a timer help people with ADHD to focus on a single task?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "The Pomodoro timer helps you focus by breaking work into manageable, short bursts (e.g., 25 minutes), making tasks less daunting and easier to start. This structured time forces you to single-task, preventing your brain from switching between activities. The ticking timer creates a sense of urgency, encouraging you to buckle down and concentrate. Regular short breaks are built in, which helps prevent burnout and refreshes your focus, making it easier to maintain attention during the work intervals. Over time, this can also help improve your attention span.",
