      {
        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Yeah, tips for finding local resources in Germany would be helpful! Also, how can a timer help people with ADHD to focus on a single task?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can a timer help people with ADHD to focus on a single task?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For finding local practical support and advocacy groups for adults with ADHD in a work setting in Germany, you should look for multi-agency groups in your locality. These groups, which include specialist ADHD teams and mental health services, are responsible for compiling comprehensive directories of information and services.\n\nTimers help people with ADHD focus on a single task by breaking down work into manageable, focused intervals (e.g., 15-25 minutes). This structured approach helps prevent boredom, aids in time management, and signals when to concentrate or take breaks, ultimately improving productivity and managing hyperfocus.",
