        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Helpful! Speaking of hyperfocus: How can a person with ADHD handle distractions while in hyperfocus?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can a person with ADHD handle distractions while in hyperfocus?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To manage distractions while in hyperfocus, use loud timers that require you to physically get up to turn them off, aiding transition to other tasks. Set time boundaries for your focused work. Involve trusted colleagues, coaches, or loved ones to gently interrupt you when needed, as a timer alone might not suffice. Also, inform people about your work blocks and availability. Practicing letting go of perfectionism can prevent getting stuck on minor details.",
