      {
        "turn": 9,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I didn\u2019t know about involving others\u2014good tip. What about meetings? How can I stay attentive during long meetings if I have ADHD?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to stay attentive in meetings while having ADHD?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To stay attentive during long meetings with ADHD, try these strategies:\n\n*   **Take Notes:** Actively taking notes, or even \"intentional fidgeting\" by writing, can help you stay engaged and provide an outlet for restlessness (P1, P3, P4, P5, P6, P11).\n*   **Record Meetings:** If permitted, record the meeting to review later, reducing the pressure to absorb everything in real-time (P5).\n*   **Minimize Distractions:** Use headphones with white noise or soothing music if appropriate for your meeting environment to block out other sounds (P1, P3, P10, P13).\n*   **Engage Actively:** Keep a list of ideas that come to you to contribute more effectively (P13).",
