      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Makes sense! Any tips for staying attentive in work meetings with ADHD? Meetings sometimes make me really tired and spaced out.",
          "user_rubrik": "How to stay attentive in meetings while having ADHD?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To stay attentive in meetings, especially when feeling tired or spaced out, try actively taking notes; this can help manage restlessness and improve focus. Engaging in \"intentional fidgeting\" like doodling, using a fidget object, or even a quiet game (if appropriate) can help channel excess energy and maintain engagement. Incorporate movement by taking brief breaks before or after the meeting, or consider standing. Listening to white noise or instrumental music can also minimize distractions and help you concentrate.",
          "citations": {
