      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Nice tips! What about handling lots of tasks at once? Any tricks for that?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to manage multiple tasks at work while having ADHD?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Handling multiple tasks with ADHD can be challenging. A key strategy is to break down large projects into smaller, manageable steps. While focusing on one task at a time is often recommended to prevent overwhelm, some find that switching between two tasks when their attention starts to diminish can actually help maintain focus and productivity. It's also crucial to avoid over-scheduling yourself by learning to say no to new obligations.",
