        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Interesting! How can a timer help people with ADHD to focus on a single task?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can a timer help people with ADHD to focus on a single task?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Timers can significantly help people with ADHD focus on a single task by providing external cues and creating a sense of urgency. They allow you to set specific work intervals, such as 15 or 30 minutes, encouraging concentrated effort during that time. Techniques like the Pomodoro method (25 minutes of work followed by a 5-minute break) utilize timers to structure focused periods. Visual timers can also make the passage of time more concrete. Additionally, timers help manage hyperfocus by signaling when it's time to transition to another task, preventing over-engagement.",
