      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Great! So how can a person with ADHD handle distractions if they're in a state of hyperfocus?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can a person with ADHD handle distractions while in hyperfocus?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To manage distractions while in a state of hyperfocus, set clear boundaries and use highly visible reminders like alarms or timers, perhaps 15 minutes before you need to shift tasks. Enlist trusted friends, family, or colleagues to gently interrupt you with a message, call, or knock when it's time to transition. You can also use a loud alarm that requires you to physically get up to switch it off, aiding your shift to another task.",
