      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That tip about needing to move to turn off the alarm is clever, I like that! Are there ways to make meetings less overwhelming for someone with ADHD? Sometimes even with alarms, meetings can feel exhausting.",
          "user_rubrik": "How to stay attentive in meetings while having ADHD?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To make meetings less overwhelming, try taking copious notes to help with restlessness and memory, or record the meeting to review later. You can also keep a list of ideas to communicate more effectively. Additionally, consider taking intermittent breaks and avoid over-scheduling yourself to manage time better.",
