      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that\u2019s more helpful! Are there techniques for keeping focus when switching between tasks? Sometimes I get super distracted.",
          "user_rubrik": "How to manage multiple tasks at work while having ADHD?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To maintain focus when switching tasks, consider single-tasking by completing one task before starting another, as multitasking can reduce speed and accuracy. The Pomodoro Technique, which involves working in focused bursts with short breaks, can also help. Some individuals find it beneficial to strategically switch between two tasks when their attention starts to wane. Additionally, taking short breaks between tasks, using fidget tools, and minimizing distractions with headphones or a quiet environment can improve concentration.",
