      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "The Pomodoro Technique keeps coming up. How can using a timer help people with ADHD to focus on a single task?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can a timer help people with ADHD to focus on a single task?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Using a timer with the Pomodoro Technique helps individuals with ADHD focus on a single task by creating short, manageable work intervals (e.g., 25 minutes). During these timed sessions, you commit to focusing solely on one task, minimizing distractions and preventing task-switching. This approach makes tasks less daunting and helps overcome resistance. The built-in short breaks allow your brain to rest and reset, preventing burnout and sustaining concentration. Over time, this method can also improve your attention span and maintain motivation by working in \"sprints.\"",
