        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Makes sense! What if someone with ADHD gets stuck in hyperfocus and forgets breaks\u2014any ways to handle that?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can a person with ADHD handle distractions while in hyperfocus?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To manage hyperfocus and ensure you take breaks, set clear time boundaries for tasks. Use timers, making alarms loud and requiring physical movement to turn off, or set them to signal a transition period before stopping. Enlist a partner, coach, or co-worker to gently interrupt you. During breaks, engage in active movement like walking or a chore, and jot down your stopping point to easily resume your work.",
