  {
    "runtag": "uva-gpt5mini-bm25-debertav3-gpt5mini",
    "type": "ikat-fragment-v1",
    "topic": "8-1",
    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m curious about ADHD management, especially at work. What strategies are there?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can ADHD be managed?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "helpful workplace strategies \u2014 practical and easy to try : 1. organize your work - break tasks into small steps, use visible checklists and a prioritized daily plan. - use timers ( pomodoro : 25 / 5 ) and calendar blocks for focused work. 2. reduce distractions - declutter your desk, put your phone away, use noise - cancelling headphones or quiet hours. - single - task where possible ; limit open tabs and notifications. 3. manage energy and alertness - schedule focused work when you \u2019 re least sleepy ; plan movement breaks ( short walks, stretches ). - use strategic caffeine, stay hydrated, and get consistent sleep. if you suddenly feel very tired, brief naps ( if allowed ) or brisk movement can help. 4. adjust your environment - ask for flexible hours, remote work days, a standing desk, or permission for short activity breaks. - use visual timers, timers on screen, and checklists to cue transitions. 5. skills & supports - adhd coaching, time - management training, or workplace accommodations via hr can help. - consider discussing assessment / treatment options with a clinician ; medication can be part of an effective plan.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0016-62-07011:1": -4.697402000427246,
            "clueweb22-en0013-25-17461:1": -5.110856056213379,
            "clueweb22-en0013-25-17461:0": -5.32601261138916,
